6mb|n|An inlet of the sea, usually smaller than a gulf, but of the same general character. ; A small body of water set off from the main body; as a compartment containing water for a wheel; the portion of a canal just outside of the gates of a lock, etc. ; A recess or indentation shaped like a bay. ; A principal compartment of the walls, roof, or other part of a building, or of the whole building, as marked off by the buttresses, vaulting, mullions of a window, etc.; one of the main divisions of any structure, as the part of a bridge between two piers. ; A compartment in a barn, for depositing hay, or grain in the stalks. ; A kind of mahogany obtained from Campeachy Bay. ; A berry, particularly of the laurel. ; The laurel tree (Laurus nobilis). Hence, in the plural, an honorary garland or crown bestowed as a prize for victory or excellence, anciently made or consisting of branches of the laurel. ; A tract covered with bay trees. ; A bank or dam to keep back water.	a:13lx,98,1;veb,80,5;1ade,70,4;1e97,64,34;1j3s,64,2;y41,63,2;e6j,58,2;1ujs,48,2;mtz,41,2;ud5,28,8;267e,17,2;vs8,15,2;mgb,13,5;1lk9,12,3;qmh,10,4~1e97,64,34;ud5,28,8;17jj,9,8;veb,80,5;mgb,13,5;qmh,10,4;1ade,70,4;12l0,9,4;1lk9,12,3;1ujs,48,2;e6j,58,2;mtz,41,2;vs8,15,2;1j3s,64,2;y41,63,2	v:13lx,98,1;226a,58,1;1gjf,56,4;y5g,20,3;16k3,9,2~1gjf,56,4;y5g,20,3;16k3,9,2;226a,58,1;13lx,98,1	V:2330,38,2;jbj,28,3;1soh,11,1~jbj,28,3;2330,38,2;1soh,11,1	n:1kex,112,5;iky,107,2;8gy,78,11;1j3s,74,4;1jtg,71,3;226a,68,2;ath,67,18;y41,53,1;mtz,51,4;1wav,48,4;1utd,44,3;1gsb,39,6;1gjf,36,1;p52,33,4;qbj,32,3~mb5,11,20;ath,67,18;8gy,78,11;6ks,16,8;obw,22,8;1gsb,39,6;1kex,112,5;p52,33,4;mtz,51,4;1wav,48,4;1j3s,74,4;qbj,32,3;28if,7,3;1utd,44,3;1jtg,71,3	N:19ph,135,2;15fu,97,1;a06,86,6;2330,74,23;1bvl,53,6;lwu,39,3;14id,36,3;1soh,21,2;yy,21,5;4fp,0,2~2330,74,23;1bvl,53,6;a06,86,6;yy,21,5;14id,36,3;lwu,39,3;4fp,0,2;1soh,21,2;19ph,135,2;15fu,97,1
